Third-party materials
---------------------
sourcedrecall's code is Apache-2.0. Setup downloads the models below, each
under its own terms; the parser and notes models are converted or trained
copies that sourcedrecall publishes on Hugging Face.

- The English parser (sourcedrecall-parser-en, the EWT archive): a
  tokenizer, multi-word token, part-of-speech, lemma and dependency model in
  the architecture of Stanza 1.14.0 (Stanford NLP Group, Apache-2.0),
  converted to ONNX by sourcedrecall. The part-of-speech and dependency
  models were trained by sourcedrecall on UD English-EWT alone (CC BY-SA
  4.0) with the GloVe vectors Stanza packages for English (Open Data
  Commons Public Domain Dedication and License) and no character language
  model (tools/stanza_ort/train_ewt.sh); the tokenizer, multi-word token
  and lemma models are Stanza's own EWT models. The weights are released
  under CC BY-SA 4.0. Installing the optional PyTorch fallback
  (`server[stanza]`) instead runs Stanza's own default English models,
  under the terms Stanza gives them (some of their training data is under
  non-commercial terms; see https://stanfordnlp.github.io/stanza/).
- BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5, MIT License.
- cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L6-v2, Apache-2.0; trained on MS MARCO,
  which Microsoft provides for non-commercial research.
- cross-encoder/nli-deberta-v3-xsmall, Apache-2.0; trained on SNLI
  (CC BY-SA 4.0) and MultiNLI.
- Qwen3-0.6B and Qwen3-1.7B (Alibaba Cloud), Apache-2.0. Modified by
  sourcedrecall: fine-tuned to write notes and quantized to int4 ONNX
  (sourcedrecall-notes-en, optional).
- WordNet 3.0, Copyright 2006 by Princeton University, under the WordNet
  License (https://wordnet.princeton.edu/license-and-commercial-use),
  downloaded by NLTK. Princeton University does not endorse this product.

Benchmark files in bench/ (not part of the software; not installed):
- bench/locomo/results hold questions, answers and retrieved passages from
  LoCoMo (snap-research/locomo), CC BY-NC 4.0: non-commercial use.
- bench/longmemeval holds question ids and the answers the reader gave on
  LongMemEval (xiaowu0162/LongMemEval), MIT License.
- Some cases in bench/false_memory quote messages from the Enron email
  corpus, made public by the US Federal Energy Regulatory Commission.
- bench/halumem holds only scores from HaluMem (MemTensor/HaluMem).
- bench/native_memory/locomo holds questions and answers from LoCoMo, as
  above (CC BY-NC 4.0); bench/native_memory/false_memory quotes the
  false-memory cases, some of them Enron emails.
- bench/factcons holds answers on MemoryAgentBench's FactConsolidation sets
  (ai-hyz/MemoryAgentBench), MIT License.
- bench/coding holds only scores and question ids from sessions in SWE-chat,
  not the sessions or the questions.
